        "v": 5,
        "title": "Filter system messages in spawn-agents history",
        "summary": "System messages are now excluded from conversation history passed to spawned agents in both sync and async handlers. This prevents parent system prompts from leaking into child agent contexts. Updated in `backend/src/tools/handlers/tool/spawn-agents.ts` and `spawn-agents-async.ts`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T10:42:51.668Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the assistant starts a new helper agent during a conversation, that helper used to receive the parent's full instruction set, including internal system-level guidance that isn't meant for child contexts. Now the system filters out those internal instructions before passing along the conversation history, so child agents only see the actual back-and-forth dialogue. The change is live today for both the immediate and background-style spawning paths.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "11d853d0aedb",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:04:09.812Z"
